    "repo": "swesmith/HIPS__autograd.ac044f0d",
    "problem_statement": "Sylvester solver VJP returns UnboundLocalError when computing gradients\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen computing gradients for the Sylvester equation solver, an `UnboundLocalError` is raised due to a variable being referenced before assignment.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport autograd.numpy as np\nfrom autograd.scipy.linalg import solve_sylvester\nfrom autograd import grad\n\n# Create test matrices\nA = np.array([[1., 2.], [3., 4.]])\nB = np.array([[5., 6.], [7., 8.]])\nQ = np.array([[9., 10.], [11., 12.]])\n\n# Try to compute gradient - this should work but raises UnboundLocalError\ndef test_func(a):\n    return np.sum(solve_sylvester(a, B, Q))\n\ngrad_func = grad(test_func)\nresult = grad_func(A)  # UnboundLocalError: local variable 'vjps' referenced before assignment\n```\n\nThe error occurs when trying to compute gradients with respect to any of the input arguments to `solve_sylvester`. The VJP (vector-Jacobian product) function has a logic error where the `vjps` list is referenced before being initialized."
  }
